Subject: lg_bsize is zero during mount, and dividing by it is undefined

Patch 0023 added a cache-coherency update to ext4_sb_write: the direct
write goes past the block cache, so the cached copy of the superblock's
home block has to be told, or the next journaled update commits stale
bytes over what was just written. Locating that cached block needs the
logical block size:

    EXT4_SUPERBLOCK_OFFSET % bdev->lg_bsize

which is a division by zero on every read-write mount, and has been since
0023 landed. ext4_mount() calls ext4_fs_init() -- which writes the
superblock to clear VALID_FS -- and only calls ext4_block_set_lb_size()
afterwards, so lg_bsize is still zero at that point.

    Core/lwext4/src/ext4_super.c:160:27: runtime error: division by zero

Harmless in practice on this target: arm64 yields zero rather than
trapping, the block index falls out as 1, and the cache is empty that
early so update_if_cached finds nothing to update. It is undefined
behaviour nonetheless, it traps on targets that do trap, and one compiler
release deciding the expression is unreachable would delete the guard
around it.

Nothing can be cached before the block layer knows its block size, so the
correct answer is to skip the update entirely.

Found by fuzzing, in the read-write pass, on a pristine e2fsck-clean seed
rather than a mutated one -- a mount, and nothing else.

--- a/src/ext4_super.c
+++ b/src/ext4_super.c
@@ -155,6 +155,16 @@
 	 * journaled superblock updates (ext4_sb_write_trans) put it there.
 	 * Tell the cached copy, or the next journaled update commits stale
 	 * bytes over what was just written. */
+
+	/* Except during mount, where the logical block size is not known yet:
+	 * ext4_mount() calls ext4_fs_init() -- which writes the superblock to
+	 * clear VALID_FS -- and only then ext4_block_set_lb_size(). lg_bsize
+	 * is zero until that call, so the modulo below is a division by zero,
+	 * on every read-write mount, since this hunk landed. Nothing can be in
+	 * the cache that early either, so there is nothing to update. */
+	if (bdev->lg_bsize == 0)
+		return EOK;
+
 	ext4_bcache_update_if_cached(bdev->bc,
 			(bdev->lg_bsize > EXT4_SUPERBLOCK_OFFSET) ? 0 : 1,
 			EXT4_SUPERBLOCK_OFFSET % bdev->lg_bsize,
